.TH DAQ-COMMON.SH 3 "2026-09-10" "mu2edaq-shifter-tools" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
daq-common.sh \- shared shell library for the Mu2e DAQ shifter tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B source "$(dirname "$0")/daq-common.sh"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B daq-common.sh
is sourced, never executed. It provides the pieces every shifter script
needs and that were previously copy-pasted into each one: the
artdaq-style option-parser block existed in four separate copies before
this library replaced it.
.PP
Its Python counterpart is
.BR mu2edaq_shifter_tools_config (3);
the two implement the same precedence and the same search path, so a
shell command and a Python command resolve a setting identically.
.PP
Sourcing it twice is a no-op: it returns early when
\fB_DAQ_COMMON_SH_LOADED\fR is already set.
.SS Locating the library
A script finds it by looking next to itself, then in \fIscripts/\fR
relative to itself (for the top-level commands), then in
\fI~/bin\fR (for an installed copy):
.PP
.RS
.nf
SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd -- "$(dirname -- "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" >/dev/null 2>&1 && pwd)"
for lib in "$SCRIPT_DIR/daq-common.sh" "$HOME/bin/daq-common.sh"; do
    [ -f "$lib" ] && { . "$lib"; break; }
done
[ -n "${_DAQ_COMMON_SH_LOADED:-}" ] || {
    echo "$0: cannot find daq-common.sh" >&2; exit 1; }
.fi
.RE
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS Diagnostics
.TP
.B daq_warn \fImessage\fR
Print \fI$DAQ_PROG: message\fR on stderr. Scripts set \fBDAQ_PROG\fR to
their own name after sourcing.
.TP
.B daq_die \fImessage\fR
\fBdaq_warn\fR, then exit with \fB$DAQ_EXIT_CODE\fR (default 1).
.TP
.B daq_status_line \fIstatus label\fR
Print \fIlabel\fB: \fRfollowed by \fBPass\fR in green when
\fIstatus\fR is 0, or \fBFail\fR in red otherwise. Used by the
login-time Kerberos and git scripts.
.SS Installation root
.TP
.B daq_repo_root
Echo the installation root: \fB$MU2EDAQ_ROOT\fR if set, else the first
ancestor of this library containing
\fIconfig/daq\-operations.example.yaml\fR, else
\fI~/daq\-shifter\-tools\fR.
.SS Environment files
.TP
.B daq_load_dotenv \fR[\fIfile\fR]
Export \fBKEY=VALUE\fR settings from the \fI.env\fR files. Variables
already present in the environment are left alone, so the environment
outranks \fI.env\fR, and an earlier file outranks a later one.
.IP
With no argument the files read are \fB$MU2EDAQ_DOTENV\fR,
\fI~/.mu2edaq/env\fR, \fI<root>/.env\fR and \fI./.env\fR.
\fI~/.mu2edaq/env\fR is where
.BR install-login.sh (1)
records \fBMU2EDAQ_ROOT\fR, which is how a command in \fI~/bin\fR finds
its config and data.
.IP
An \fBexport\fR prefix and one layer of matching quotes are tolerated;
blanks, comments and keys that are not shell identifiers are ignored.
.SS Configuration files
.TP
.B daq_config_path
Echo the config search path, one absolute directory per line:
\fB$MU2EDAQ_CONFIG_DIR\fR, \fI$PWD/config\fR, \fI<root>/config\fR,
\fI~/.config/mu2edaq\fR, \fI/etc/mu2edaq\fR.
.TP
.B daq_config_file \fIname\fR [\fIexplicit\fR]
Echo the path of a config file. A non-empty \fIexplicit\fR is used
as-is, with a leading \fB~/\fR expanded, and must exist. Otherwise
\fIname\fR is looked for on \fBdaq_config_path\fR. Returns 1 and prints
the search path on stderr when nothing is found.
.IP
The tilde expansion is done explicitly because the pattern in
\fB${var#~/}\fR is itself tilde-expanded by bash, which is what broke
the original scripts' default config path.
.SS Python
.TP
.B daq_python
Echo the interpreter to use: \fI<root>/venv/bin/python\fR if the venv
has been bootstrapped, else \fB$PYTHON\fR, else \fBpython3\fR.
.TP
.B daq_require_python_deps
Return 0 if \fBPyYAML\fR and \fBclick\fR are importable, trying
\fI<root>/src\fR on \fBPYTHONPATH\fR as well. Otherwise warn, naming
\fBbootstrap.sh\fR, and return non-zero.
.TP
.B daq_run_tool \fImodule console\fR [\fIargs\fR...]
Run one tool from the package, preferring the venv's console script,
then one on \fBPATH\fR, then \fBpython \-m
mu2edaq_shifter_tools.\fImodule\fR with \fI<root>/src\fR on
\fBPYTHONPATH\fR. That last fallback is what lets an un-installed
checkout work.
.TP
.B daq_read_config \fR[\fIargs\fR...]
Shorthand for \fBdaq_run_tool read_config daq\-read\-config\fR. This is
how every shell command reads the operations YAML.
.SS Options
.TP
.B daq_script_opts \fR[\fIprog\fR]
Echo the contents of \fB$<PROG>_OPTS\fR so options can come from the
environment as well as the command line. The name is the program with
\fB.\fR and \fB\-\fR mapped to \fB_\fR and upper-cased, so
\fBstart\-daq.sh\fR reads \fBSTART_DAQ_SH_OPTS\fR. The pre-rename name
(\fBSTART_DAQ_OPTS\fR) is used only when the modern one is unset.
.IP
Scripts apply it as:
.IP
.RS
.nf
eval set -- $(daq_script_opts start-daq.sh) '"$@"'
.fi
.RE
.SS Confirmation
.TP
.B daq_confirm \fIassume_yes prompt\fR
Return 0 immediately when \fIassume_yes\fR is \fB1\fR, otherwise prompt
and return 0 only on \fBy\fR or \fByes\fR. Used before anything that
can interrupt data taking.
.SH VARIABLES
.TP
.B _DAQ_COMMON_SH_LOADED
Set to 1 once the library is sourced. Also the flag a script checks to
confirm the library was found.
.TP
.B DAQ_PROG
The calling script's name, used in diagnostics and as the default for
\fBdaq_script_opts\fR.
.TP
.B DAQ_EXIT_CODE
Exit status used by \fBdaq_die\fR. Default 1.
.SH PORTABILITY
The library and the scripts that use it avoid \fBmapfile\fR and
unguarded empty-array expansion, both of which fail under the bash 3.2
that ships as the system shell on macOS. Empty arrays are expanded as
\fB${a[@]+"${a[@]}"}\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
A minimal command built on the library:
.PP
.RS
.nf
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -u
SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd -- "$(dirname -- "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" >/dev/null 2>&1 && pwd)"
. "$SCRIPT_DIR/daq-common.sh"

DAQ_PROG="my-tool.sh"
daq_load_dotenv

config="${MU2EDAQ_CONFIG:-}"
partition="${MU2EDAQ_PARTITION:-partition_0}"

eval set -- $(daq_script_opts my-tool.sh) '"$@"'
while [ -n "${1:-}" ]; do
    case "$1" in
        -c|--config)    shift; config="${1:-}";;
        -z|--partition) shift; partition="${1:-}";;
        *)              daq_die "unknown option: $1";;
    esac
    shift
done

config_file="$(daq_config_file daq-operations.yaml "$config")" || exit 1
daq_read_config --config "$config_file" -z "$partition" active-envs
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq_shifter_tools_config (3),
.BR mu2edaq_shifter_tools (3),
.BR daq-read-config (1),
.BR install-login.sh (1),
.BR bootstrap.sh (1)
